<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48536" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tŏnus</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόνος.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The stretching</i>, <i>straining</i>
			of a rope: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mollior, vehementior,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10, 10, 6</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>the sound</i>, <i>tone</i>, of an instrument, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 2, 1 <i>med.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart.
				Cap. 9, § 959</span></i>.—Of the tone of
			a syllable, <i>accent</i>, Nigid. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell.
				13, 25, 1 sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Like our <i>tone</i>, in painting, of the natural color of an object,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				35, 5, 11, § 29</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> For tonitrus, <i>thunder</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 2, 56, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
